<title>USA: Central U.S. carlot pork 1115 CST - USDA.</title>
<headline>Central U.S. carlot pork 1115 CST - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fresh retail cuts not established; sknd. hams 17-20 lbs 2.00-4.00 higher, 20-26 lbs 1.00-2.00 higher; sdls. bellies 12-14 lbs 2.00 higher; trimmings steady. Trading slow, with light to moderate demand and light offerings.</p>
<p>Loads PORK CUTS	     :     15.1</p>
<p>Loads TRIM/PROCESS PORK   :	4.0</p>
<p>	    Weight/lb  Lds   Price Range	  Wghtd avg</p>
<p>HAM, SKINNED, SELECTED</p>
<p>Fresh	17-20#    5.0   88.00 -  92.00	 90.20</p>
<p>Fresh	20-26#    6.0   71.50 -  77.00	 75.25</p>
<p>BELLY, SDLS, SKIN-ON, FRESH</p>
<p>Fresh	12-14#    2.0		64.00	 64.00</p>
<p>	    Weight/lb  Lds   Price Range	  Wghtd avg</p>
<p>PORK TRIMMINGS/BONELESS PROCESSING PORK (CHEMICAL LEAN):</p>
<p>Combo 42%  Fresh     1.0		42.00	 42.00</p>
<p>Combo 72%  Fresh     3.0		66.00	 66.00</p>
<p>		Weight/lb    Lds  Price Range	   Wghtd avg</p>
<p>LOINS, REGULAR, FRESH</p>
<p>		18-22# *    2.0  108.00 - 109.00	108.50</p>
<p>1/4&quot; Trim   18-22#	2.0  126.00 - 127.00	126.50</p>
<p>BNLS SIRLOIN .75-1#     0.13	    133.00	133.00</p>
<p>Note! (*) Reflects 1/4&quot; or 1/8&quot; trimmed product brought back to a regular commodity basis.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720--</p>
